{"team":"TEN","col":"#4FC3E8","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":59.6,"adot":7.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Ground-First Machine</h2><p>The backfield runs through one man \u2014 <strong>Tony Pollard</strong> absorbs <strong>70% of the carries</strong> (league ~59%), a true bell-cow share that makes his rushing volume among the safest floors in the sport when the script cooperates.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Run identity is the through-line here: TEN call pass on <strong>-5%</strong> of snaps relative to what the situation expects (league -2%), and when they get ahead they lean even harder on the ground \u2014 just 38% pass on early downs with a lead. This is a ball-control operation built to shorten games.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 62% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 39% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they stay aggressive, throwing <strong>54%</strong> of the time, which puts scoring equity on <strong>Wan'Dale Robinson</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p>They surrender <strong>125 rushing</strong> and <strong>219 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 44 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.53/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They lock down backs out of the backfield \u2014 just 13 rec yds/game (vs ~18); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.53/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Tony Pollard</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Cam Ward","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":11,"props":{"Comp":16.7,"Att":27.75,"Pass Yds":162.11,"Pass TD":0.81,"INT":0.34,"Rush Yds":12.4},"d":{"completions":16.7,"attempts":27.75,"pass_yards":162.11,"pass_td":0.81,"interceptions":0.34,"rush_att":2.63,"rush_yards":12.4}}],"RB":[{"name":"Tony Pollard","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":27,"props":{"Rush Att":21.21,"Rush Yds":95.1,"Tgt":2.91,"Rec":2.31,"Rec Yds":15.74},"d":{"rush_att":21.21,"rush_yards":95.1,"targets":2.91,"receptions":2.31,"rec_yards":15.74,"rec_td":0.03}},{"name":"Tyjae Spears","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":20,"props":{"Rush Att":5.46,"Rush Yds":22.37,"Tgt":4.81,"Rec":3.34,"Rec Yds":22.65},"d":{"rush_att":5.46,"rush_yards":22.37,"targets":4.81,"receptions":3.34,"rec_yards":22.65,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Nicholas Singleton","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":14,"props":{"Rush Att":4.15,"Rush Yds":17.36,"Tgt":1.58,"Rec":1.06,"Rec Yds":7.37},"d":{"rush_att":4.15,"rush_yards":17.36,"targets":1.58,"receptions":1.06,"rec_yards":7.37,"rec_td":0.04}},{"name":"Julius Chestnut","slot":"RB4","starter":false,"td":8,"props":{"Rush Att":3.34,"Rush Yds":13.11,"Tgt":1.6,"Rec":1.04,"Rec Yds":8.02},"d":{"rush_att":3.34,"rush_yards":13.11,"targets":1.6,"receptions":1.04,"rec_yards":8.02,"rec_td":0.03}}],"WR":[{"name":"Carnell Tate","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":21,"props":{"Tgt":6.69,"Rec":4.24,"Rec Yds":53.26,"Rec TD":0.24},"d":{"targets":6.69,"receptions":4.24,"rec_yards":53.26,"rec_td":0.24}},{"name":"Wan'Dale Robinson","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":19,"props":{"Tgt":10.54,"Rec":7.35,"Rec Yds":68.07,"Rec TD":0.21},"d":{"targets":10.54,"receptions":7.35,"rec_yards":68.07,"rec_td":0.21}},{"name":"Ca